*  VISIT_driver - exercises the VISIT module's published functions VISIT(SON,SIGN),
*  DATA(S) and FIELD(DT,I).  The module ships no header comment, so this drives
*  the published signatures only: VISIT's own body requires the caller to supply
*  PROCESS(SON) and uses the MARK field that its overridden DATA(S) appends.
-INCLUDE "VISIT.sno"
        DATA('NODE(LEFT,RIGHT)')
        DEFINE('PROCESS(X)')                    :(MAIN)
PROCESS OUTPUT  =  'visit ' DATATYPE(X)          :(RETURN)
MAIN    T  =  NODE(NODE('a','b'),'c')
        VISIT(T,1)
        OUTPUT  =  'done'
END
